meta {
  name: 44 Get Order Grouped Samples (Overview)
  type: http
  seq: 44
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/order/{{orderId}}/grouped
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("single order group (or null when no samples)", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    if (d) {
      expect(d).to.have.property("orderId");
      expect(d).to.have.property("groupingMode");
      expect(d).to.have.property("groups");
      expect(d).to.have.property("sampleIds");
      if (d.groups.length) {
        expect(d.groups[0]).to.have.property("barcode");
        expect(d.groups[0]).to.have.property("sampleIds");
      }
    }
  });
}

docs {
  Grouped accession samples for a **single order** — the same order-first
  grouping `40 List Grouped Samples` produces (keyed on the tenant's current
  grouping mode via `GET/PUT /tenant/accession-settings/grouping-mode`), but
  scoped to ONE order id instead of a page of orders. Powers the Product Overview
  modal's grouped Test Details on `/registration/create`, so its groups /
  barcodes / action-scope mirror `/accession/inhouse-orders` exactly.

  Scoped by tenant + order id only (no branch filter): the modal always targets a
  specific order the caller just created/opened.

  ## Returns

  A single `InHouseOrderGroup` (same shape as one element of `40`'s `data[]`):

  - `orderId` + `order` — the order id and its header context (patient, referral).
  - `groupingMode` — the tenant's current mode (FE layout hint).
  - `sampleIds[]` — all sample ids in the order.
  - `groups[]` — the final (barcode) groups within the order; each carries
    `groupKey`, `barcode` (or null → "No barcode"), `department`, `sampleLabel`,
    `samples[]` (each with `tatStatus` + `departmentName`) and the flat
    `sampleIds[]` a group action targets.

  Resolves to **`null`** when the order has no generated samples yet (e.g. a
  DRAFT / non-diagnostic order) — the FE then falls back to its flat per-item
  table. The group's `sampleIds` feed `POST /orders/:id/collect-group`.
}
